---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import BookCta from "../components/BookCta.astro";
import { showRealtorQuote } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="AI for Realtors, Without the Hype · Josh Robinson"
      description="Told to use AI but not sure where to start? I help agents and brokerages pick what's worth it, set it up, and learn to use it safely."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
      <p class="kicker">examples / real-estate</p>
      <h1>AI for Realtors, without the hype</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        You've been told to use AI. Here's someone who will sit down with you,
        figure out what's actually worth it for your business, set it up, and
        show you how to use it.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="why-title">
        <h2 id="why-title">Why this page exists</h2>
        <p>
          In real estate, the message to "use AI" is everywhere: conference
          stages, brokerage meetings, software pitches. What's usually missing
          is someone who shows agents how to actually get started.
        </p>
        <p>
          If that sounds familiar, you're not behind. You just haven't had
          anyone show you yet.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="help-title">
        <h2 id="help-title">Where AI can help an agent or a team</h2>
        <p class="example-label">// examples</p>
        <p>Ideas to show what's possible. We'll pick what fits how you work.</p>
        <ul class="deliverables">
          <li>
            <strong>Listing descriptions and marketing.</strong> Get a solid
            first draft from your notes and photos, then make it yours. You stay
            in charge of every word, including fair housing language.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Follow-up that doesn't slip.</strong> Draft personal
            follow-ups after showings and open houses, and keep your CRM up to
            date without the typing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Making long documents readable.</strong> Turn inspection
            reports and disclosures into a first-pass summary you review before
            sharing with clients.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Deadlines and checklists.</strong> Keep every transaction's
            dates and to-dos in front of you so nothing gets missed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Market updates and social posts.</strong> Turn your local
            knowledge into a regular newsletter or posts in a fraction of the
            time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>For brokerages and teams.</strong> Shared tools, simple
            rules about client data, and training so every agent uses AI the
            same, safe way.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="together-title">
        <h2 id="together-title">How we'd work together</h2>
        <p>Same three steps as any business:</p>
        <ol class="deliverables">
          <li>
            <strong>Explore.</strong> We look at your week and find the two or
            three things AI should take off your plate.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Set up.</strong> I set up the tools and connect them to what
            you already use, like your CRM and email.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Train.</strong> I show you, or your whole team, how to use
            them, check them, and stay on the right side of the rules.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="caution-title">
        <h2 id="caution-title">A word of caution</h2>
        <p>
          AI gets things wrong, and in real estate some mistakes are costly.
          Part of what I teach is how to check AI's work, what never to paste
          into it, and where a human always signs off.
        </p>
      </section>

      {showRealtorQuote && (
        <section aria-label="Realtor quote">
          <blockquote />
        </section>
      )}

      <BookCta heading="Came back from a conference wondering where to start? Let's talk." />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
